cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying artifacts, please cite both the
  software (this file) and the associated paper (see preferred-citation).
title: >-
  An eXplainable Approach to Abstractive Text Summarization Using External
  Knowledge: A Novel Framework for Financial Domain Applications
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation, configuration files, prompts and evaluation code for a
  FIBO-grounded hybrid neural-symbolic framework for explainable abstractive
  summarization of financial documents, integrating five explainability components
  (MESA, CAUSAL-EXPLAIN, ADAPT-EVAL, INTERPRETABLE-CONSENSUS, TEMPORAL-EXPLAIN).
  Trained model checkpoints and experimental logs from the original runs were not
  retained; see README.md for what is and is not reproducible.
